# Database Conventions

## Per-service database isolation
Each service owns exactly one database. Never add a foreign key or a JPA relationship that crosses service boundaries.

| Service | Owns |
|---|---|
| Ingestion | `ingestion-db` — raw staging tables only |
| Employee Profile | `profile-db` — curated `training_attendance`, `assessment_records`, `employee_milestone_progress` |
| Risk Engine | `risk-db` — `risk_assessments`, `risk_reviews` |
| Rule Management | `rules-db` |
| Intervention | `intervention-db` |
| Reporting | `reporting-db` — CDC-fed read model, never written by domain services |
| Consent | `consent-db` — `consents`, `data_erasure_requests` |
| Audit | `audit-db` — append-only `audit_log` |

## Outbox table — required in every service that publishes events
```sql
CREATE TABLE {service}_outbox (
    outbox_id     BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    tenant_id     VARCHAR   NOT NULL,
    aggregate_id  VARCHAR   NOT NULL,
    event_type    VARCHAR   NOT NULL,
    payload       BYTEA     NOT NULL,  -- Protobuf-serialised
    created_at    TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    published_at  TIMESTAMP
);
CREATE INDEX idx_{service}_outbox_unpublished ON {service}_outbox (published_at)
    WHERE published_at IS NULL;
```

## Required indexes
Every table with a `tenant_id` column must have a composite index `(tenant_id, ...)`. See `architecture/02-database.md` for the full index list.

## Idempotency key uniqueness
```sql
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_ingest_idempotency ON ingestion_jobs (tenant_id, idempotency_key);
```

## Naming conventions
- Tables: `snake_case`, plural nouns — `risk_assessments`, `training_attendance`
- PKs: `{table_singular}_id` — `risk_id`, `attendance_id`
- Timestamps: `created_at`, `updated_at` on every table
- Soft deletes: use `status` column — never hard-delete domain records

## Migrations
Use Flyway. Migration files named `V{n}__{description}.sql`. Never edit an existing migration — create a new one.

## Reporting DB is read-only to application code
The `reporting-db` is populated exclusively by the CDC Debezium consumer. Application services must never write to it directly.
